# Only what the page renders ships, and this is the allowlist it reads: README.md ·
# assets/svg/{header,divider,footer}.svg · assets/svg/icons/*.svg · the hand-kept
# assets/svg/brands/amazonaws.svg — every generated file in both a dark and a `-light` version.
# Ignoring any of those breaks the live profile. Why the rest is local-only, and what shipping
# so little costs, are recorded in the `mathewmusango` skill.
#
# Two traps, both already hit: **gitignore does not untrack a file that is already tracked**, so
# each entry here was also `git rm --cached`'d; and `.github/` + `LICENSE` are kept even though
# they are not render inputs, because a workflow only runs once it is committed.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# Local-only: the generator, its input lists, the working docs and the preview sheets.
.preview/
DEVELOPING.md
TODO.md
data/
scripts/
assets/svg/brands/README.md
